1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,000
<i> A Bolagos police officer</i>

2
00:00:02,167 --> 00:00:04,367
<i>is believed to have died
in an explosion</i>

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,833
<i>along the Bolagos
Service Road tonight.</i>

4
00:00:06,967 --> 00:00:09,300
<i>Major Miguel Delgado of the
Bolagos Police</i>

5
00:00:09,433 --> 00:00:11,367
<i> is believed to be the victim.</i>

6
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:13,367
<i>In an interview with Bolagos
Police Chief Lansang,</i>

7
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:15,933
<i>at first glance, it seemed like
an accident.</i>

8
00:00:16,067 --> 00:00:17,600
<i>But there is evidence suggesting</i>

9
00:00:17,733 --> 00:00:19,267
<i> a possible foul play.</i>

10
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:20,700
<i>There are skid marks
on the road.</i>

11
00:00:20,833 --> 00:00:22,133
<i> It looks like he lost control</i>

12
00:00:22,267 --> 00:00:23,500
<i> before crashing into the wall.</i>

13
00:00:23,633 --> 00:00:25,767
<i>We found shell casings
at the crash site.</i>

14
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,933
<i>There was a shooter,
it's a targeted attack.</i>

15
00:00:28,067 --> 00:00:29,800
<i> Are you sure Delgado is dead?</i>

16
00:00:29,933 --> 00:00:31,033
<i>I was only a few meters away
from his car</i>

17
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:32,233
<i> when it exploded.</i>

18
00:00:32,367 --> 00:00:34,200
<i>I'll increase your payment
for a job well done.</i>

19
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:35,367
<i> If he hadn't left,</i>

20
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:36,633
<i> this wouldn't have happened!</i>

21
00:00:36,767 --> 00:00:40,433
<i>He said this was going to be
his last mission.</i>

22
00:00:40,567 --> 00:00:41,500
<i> You know, Andrew is right.</i>

23
00:00:41,633 --> 00:00:43,433
<i>We don't really know
that Korean guy.</i>

24
00:00:43,567 --> 00:00:44,567
<i> It's me, Jin Ho.</i>

25
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:45,633
<i> Jin Ho, what happened to you?</i>

26
00:00:45,767 --> 00:00:46,767
<i> Where are you?</i>

27
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:48,033
<i>Jin Ho, there's something
you need to know.</i>

28
00:00:48,167 --> 00:00:49,733
<i>This is the last time
we'll talk.</i>

29
00:00:49,867 --> 00:00:51,533
<i> Joey's father is dead, Jin Ho.</i>

30
00:00:51,667 --> 00:00:53,667
<i> That's why I don't believe it.</i>

31
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:54,933
<i> What do you mean, Joey?</i>

32
00:00:55,067 --> 00:00:56,933
<i>I have a really strong feeling
that Dad is still alive.</i>

33
00:00:57,067 --> 00:00:59,100
<i>What did Major Delgado's body
look like</i>

34
00:00:59,233 --> 00:01:00,233
<i> after the explosion?</i>

35
00:01:00,367 --> 00:01:01,800
<i> Actually, we didn't see it.</i>

36
00:01:01,933 --> 00:01:04,333
<i>No one saw it except the police?</i>

37
00:01:04,467 --> 00:01:05,933
<i>The people doing the autopsy
probably know</i>

38
00:01:06,067 --> 00:01:07,133
<i> what they're doing,</i>

39
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,500
<i>so they should know how long
the tests will take.</i>

40
00:01:09,633 --> 00:01:11,733
<i>So why can't they give us a
definite time</i>

41
00:01:11,867 --> 00:01:13,900
<i> as to when we can see Dad?</i>

42
00:01:14,033 --> 00:01:15,133
<i> Nothing?</i>

43
00:01:15,267 --> 00:01:17,333
<i> What are you doing here?</i>

44
00:01:17,467 --> 00:01:19,567
<i> Why his body isn't here?</i>

45
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:39,933
Answer me!

46
00:01:40,067 --> 00:01:41,433
Where is my father?

47
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:44,333
Ma'am, please wait.

48
00:01:44,467 --> 00:01:45,600
It's not here.

49
00:01:45,733 --> 00:01:46,767
This is Room 1.

50
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:49,567
Major Delgado
is in the other room.

51
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:51,767
Then why didn't you say that
right away?

52
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:53,967
It's like you're hiding
where he is.

53
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:55,467
I want to see my father!

54
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:56,767
That's enough!

55
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:58,267
Follow me.

56
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:08,433
That was a restricted area.

57
00:02:08,567 --> 00:02:10,467
You weren't supposed
to go in there.

58
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:11,800
Do you know you could be charged

59
00:02:11,933 --> 00:02:14,267
with obstruction of justice for
what you did?

60
00:02:14,433 --> 00:02:15,833
Chief, if you're not
hiding anything,

61
00:02:15,967 --> 00:02:18,833
then why don't you just show us
my father's body?

62
00:02:18,967 --> 00:02:20,967
The police will not bend

63
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:23,800
to anyone's whims, Joey.

64
00:02:23,933 --> 00:02:26,700
You'll get your answers,
but not like this.

65
00:02:26,833 --> 00:02:29,333
Don't let your emotions
take over everything.

66
00:02:29,467 --> 00:02:30,867
There's a proper process.

67
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,567
I think you're smart enough
to understand that.

68
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:35,067
Go home.

69
00:02:35,567 --> 00:02:36,600
Just wait for us to release

70
00:02:36,733 --> 00:02:39,700
your father's body to you
and Clarissa.

71
00:02:55,267 --> 00:02:56,567
Andrew, Dad's body isn't there

72
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:58,567
and they can't show anything.

73
00:03:00,367 --> 00:03:03,267
Maybe it's in another room

74
00:03:03,967 --> 00:03:06,067
like the medico-legal said,
right?

75
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,800
Then why won't they show it?

76
00:03:07,933 --> 00:03:09,467
Why does it seem like
they're hiding something?

77
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:12,433
Joey, there could be
many reasons.

78
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:17,033
Protocol, investigation,
case sensitivity,

79
00:03:17,167 --> 00:03:20,767
or maybe the state
of your father's remains.

80
00:03:22,067 --> 00:03:24,167
Or maybe there are no remains,
no body...

81
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:25,367
because Dad is still alive.

82
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:26,867
He's not dead.

83
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,100
Why would the police do that,
right?

84
00:03:30,033 --> 00:03:32,967
Why would they hide the fact
that your father is alive?

85
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:35,900
That would be a huge conspiracy.

86
00:03:36,033 --> 00:03:37,400
This isn't a movie.

87
00:03:37,533 --> 00:03:39,200
If your father is alive...

88
00:03:40,233 --> 00:03:42,600
why hasn't he come home to you?

89
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:49,167
I don't know.

90
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:52,567
I just have a strong feeling.

91
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:54,867
I believe Dad is still alive.

92
00:03:55,567 --> 00:03:57,300
If you don't want to believe it,
then don't.

93
00:03:57,433 --> 00:03:59,233
I'll be the one to find him.

94
00:04:02,767 --> 00:04:05,700
If only I knew where he went,

95
00:04:06,167 --> 00:04:07,433
it would be easier to find him.

96
00:04:07,567 --> 00:04:09,533
But they didn't say anything.

97
00:04:20,933 --> 00:04:22,267
Why?

98
00:04:23,533 --> 00:04:25,900
Do you know where Dad went?

99
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:29,200
<i> Here's the coordination letter</i>

100
00:04:29,333 --> 00:04:31,067
<i>and letter order you requested.</i>

101
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:33,467
<i>I've also contacted drug
enforcement</i>

102
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:37,267
<i>at the regional office in the
North, in the town of Valmora.</i>

103
00:04:37,667 --> 00:04:40,733
<i>Make a courtesy call
to their regional director.</i>

104
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:44,000
<i>Wait, do Joey
and Miss Clarissa know</i>

105
00:04:44,133 --> 00:04:45,233
<i> you're going there?</i>

106
00:04:45,367 --> 00:04:47,100
<i> They support me.</i>

107
00:04:47,733 --> 00:04:50,000
<i>But there are still many things
they don't know.</i>

108
00:04:50,833 --> 00:04:53,233
<i>That's why they can't know
what you heard.</i>

109
00:04:53,367 --> 00:04:56,033
<i>What I'm saying is, protect her</i>

110
00:04:56,167 --> 00:04:58,533
<i>from things that could put her
in danger.</i>

111
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:01,800
I heard...

112
00:05:03,767 --> 00:05:06,000
Major was given a mission order

113
00:05:06,867 --> 00:05:08,967
for a mission in the North,

114
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:10,900
in the town of Valmora.

115
00:05:12,567 --> 00:05:14,233
The town of Valmora?

116
00:05:14,367 --> 00:05:16,000
That's huge, right?

117
00:05:16,133 --> 00:05:18,367
Where do we even start
looking for him?

118
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:22,400
If there's one person who knows

119
00:05:22,533 --> 00:05:24,267
where he went...

120
00:05:26,133 --> 00:05:27,833
it's Lansang.

121
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:56,400
Hello?

122
00:05:56,533 --> 00:05:58,400
<i> You're at the gym again?</i>

123
00:05:58,533 --> 00:05:59,800
What's wrong with that?

124
00:05:59,933 --> 00:06:01,033
This is mine too.

125
00:06:01,167 --> 00:06:03,067
I put some money to this place.

126
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:06,233
Besides, I needed a break.

127
00:06:06,767 --> 00:06:08,933
I can't take being cooped up
anymore.

128
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:10,500
Cooped up?

129
00:06:10,633 --> 00:06:12,067
Yeah, you heard me.

130
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,933
Don't worry, I'll be back soon.

131
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,267
Peter.

132
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:25,533
Jin Ho...

133
00:06:25,667 --> 00:06:27,600
Why did we have to meet here of
all places?

134
00:06:28,267 --> 00:06:29,467
So random!

135
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:31,233
What I'm about to say
is serious.

136
00:06:31,367 --> 00:06:33,667
My friend owns this place

137
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:35,733
and I can't go too far.

138
00:06:36,233 --> 00:06:37,567
Why?

139
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:39,267
Just tell me about
Joey's father.

140
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:40,867
What happened?

141
00:06:56,567 --> 00:06:58,700
- Chief.
- Oh, Mr. Dizon.

142
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:00,533
Why?

143
00:07:00,667 --> 00:07:02,200
Can I talk to you?

144
00:07:03,133 --> 00:07:06,233
It's about Major Delgado's case.

145
00:07:08,367 --> 00:07:10,367
We already posted an update.

146
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:12,033
You can base it on that.

147
00:07:12,167 --> 00:07:13,600
This is different, Chief.

148
00:07:13,733 --> 00:07:17,567
What I'm thinking
is an exclusive interview.

149
00:07:27,267 --> 00:07:30,667
Basically, Major Delgado's case
will just be the springboard,

150
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:32,267
but what we'll really highlight,
Chief,

151
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:35,500
are your successful operations
here in Bolagos.

152
00:07:35,867 --> 00:07:37,433
A way to boost your image.

153
00:07:44,333 --> 00:07:45,933
Delgado...

154
00:07:56,367 --> 00:07:58,067
Major Miguel Delgado...

155
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:00,767
To proceed to the Northern part
of the Philippines,

156
00:08:01,233 --> 00:08:02,033
City of Valmora,

157
00:08:02,167 --> 00:08:03,467
in connection with the
performance

158
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:05,300
of official duties

159
00:08:05,433 --> 00:08:07,367
to conduct an investigation...

160
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:10,033
Let's admit it,

161
00:08:10,167 --> 00:08:12,167
the people of Bolagos are really
starting to lose trust

162
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,133
in the police.

163
00:08:15,133 --> 00:08:17,100
Right? And of course,
you're the chief.

164
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:19,133
That's not good for your image.

165
00:08:19,567 --> 00:08:21,533
An exclusive interview?

166
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:23,667
What exactly do you have
in mind?

167
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:25,833
Chief, a lot.

168
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:28,433
We'll start from...

169
00:08:28,567 --> 00:08:31,733
the time you transferred
here to Bolagos.

170
00:08:34,367 --> 00:08:35,733
Hmm.

171
00:08:44,167 --> 00:08:45,967
Area of operation:

172
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:48,200
Northern part
of the Philippines.

173
00:08:48,933 --> 00:08:50,067
Target:

174
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:53,067
Berdugo, a drug syndicate.

175
00:08:53,667 --> 00:08:55,467
Chief, once we establish

176
00:08:55,633 --> 00:08:58,467
your successful operations here
in Bolagos,

177
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:01,333
then it will be easier for the
people

178
00:09:01,467 --> 00:09:04,833
to trust you and
the Bolagos Police again.

179
00:09:05,700 --> 00:09:07,500
Hmm, that sounds good.

180
00:09:08,267 --> 00:09:10,067
That would help a lot.

181
00:09:10,667 --> 00:09:12,900
So, Chief, when can we start?

182
00:09:14,433 --> 00:09:15,733
I'll think about it first.

183
00:09:15,867 --> 00:09:17,367
Excuse me.

184
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:19,300
Chief, actually...

185
00:09:19,433 --> 00:09:21,367
do you think we can start
tomorrow?

186
00:09:21,933 --> 00:09:23,233
And maybe we can begin with

187
00:09:23,367 --> 00:09:28,300
the case of Major Miguel
Delgado.

188
00:09:30,767 --> 00:09:31,800
Ah...

189
00:09:33,467 --> 00:09:36,167
I know, Chief, that it's a bit
hard to decide right now,

190
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:38,033
but I think...

191
00:09:38,167 --> 00:09:40,333
this will really be
good for Bolagos

192
00:09:40,467 --> 00:09:42,833
and for your reputation.

193
00:09:44,667 --> 00:09:47,867
All right.

194
00:09:57,333 --> 00:09:59,700
They chased Tito Miguel's car.

195
00:09:59,833 --> 00:10:03,400
In the end, it crashed
and exploded.

196
00:10:04,267 --> 00:10:06,867
I have a strong feeling it was
the syndicate...

197
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,667
the ones who went after him.

198
00:10:09,767 --> 00:10:12,467
[SPEAKS IN KOREAN]

199
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:14,700
What did you say?

200
00:10:14,833 --> 00:10:18,000
I said I feel bad for Joey...

201
00:10:18,933 --> 00:10:20,100
because she worked so hard

202
00:10:20,233 --> 00:10:22,233
to get her father out of prison,

203
00:10:22,367 --> 00:10:24,767
and this is how it ended.

204
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:26,833
Exactly.

205
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:30,900
We should go see her.

206
00:10:31,033 --> 00:10:33,067
She needs us right now, Jin Ho.

207
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,400
I can't.

208
00:10:35,567 --> 00:10:37,100
I can't stay long.

209
00:10:37,533 --> 00:10:38,967
But why?

210
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:41,367
And where are you really
staying now?

211
00:10:41,500 --> 00:10:42,300
We thought

212
00:10:42,433 --> 00:10:43,667
that after you caught
Theresa Park,

213
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:44,867
you went back to Korea,

214
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,967
but you're actually here

215
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:49,033
No.

216
00:10:49,167 --> 00:10:51,033
I haven't followed her yet.

217
00:10:51,633 --> 00:10:53,667
All right, let's call Joey.

218
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:56,433
You're right, Andrew.

219
00:10:56,567 --> 00:10:58,300
Dad was sent to the town of
Valmora

220
00:10:58,433 --> 00:10:59,800
for his mission.

221
00:10:59,933 --> 00:11:02,633
Then Berdugo was supposed to
take over there

222
00:11:02,767 --> 00:11:05,533
for his drug operations
in the North.

223
00:11:05,667 --> 00:11:06,967
I remember...

224
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:08,900
That's exactly what our sources
were saying

225
00:11:09,067 --> 00:11:11,033
even before anything happened
to your father.

226
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:15,633
If Dad is alive,

227
00:11:16,367 --> 00:11:19,067
he'll definitely
go to that town.

228
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:20,667
I know him.

229
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:22,300
He won't stop until the people

230
00:11:22,433 --> 00:11:24,100
who need to be jailed
are behind bars.

231
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:25,567
Okay...

232
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:27,500
Joey, don't tell me
you're going there?

233
00:11:27,633 --> 00:11:29,000
That's insane.

234
00:11:30,267 --> 00:11:31,000
Why are you calling it insane?

235
00:11:31,133 --> 00:11:32,200
What's insane about that?

236
00:11:32,333 --> 00:11:34,700
You're not even sure
about your theory yet.

237
00:11:34,833 --> 00:11:36,467
Okay, what if
they suddenly release

238
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:37,667
your father's body to you

239
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:40,100
with official confirmation
that it's really him?

240
00:11:40,633 --> 00:11:42,300
You know what's true?

241
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:44,567
That's what's more insane to me.

242
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:46,833
Because there's only one thing
my mind,

243
00:11:46,967 --> 00:11:48,733
my heart, and even my gut
are telling me...

244
00:11:48,867 --> 00:11:50,767
that Dad is alive,
and I will find him.

245
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:52,033
But, Joey...

246
00:11:52,167 --> 00:11:54,233
Andrew, you can't stop me.

247
00:11:54,367 --> 00:11:56,067
Can you just stop
worrying about me?

248
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,700
Stop thinking about me?

249
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:00,333
Because you won't be
able to stop

250
00:12:00,467 --> 00:12:03,000
this so-called insanity
of mine anyway.

251
00:12:03,133 --> 00:12:04,700
And I won't bother you.

252
00:12:04,833 --> 00:12:07,600
I won't ask for your help
or anyone else's.

253
00:12:25,533 --> 00:12:27,633
She must be busy.
No signal.

254
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:32,500
Maybe she's shutting herself off
because she's sad.

255
00:12:33,733 --> 00:12:36,000
You know, I really want
to go see Joey.

256
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:38,767
But I've got so much work
at the shop.

257
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:40,467
I'm already trying
to speed things up.

258
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:44,533
You're really in love with her,
Peter.

259
00:12:45,833 --> 00:12:47,133
So what?

260
00:12:47,267 --> 00:12:49,233
I don't have a chance with her.

261
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:51,400
She only sees me as a friend.

262
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:53,733
You actually have
a better chance.

263
00:12:54,967 --> 00:12:56,133
No.

264
00:12:56,267 --> 00:12:57,267
Really?

265
00:12:57,400 --> 00:13:00,067
Alam ko sabi mo nun
bro code-bro code,

266
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:01,467
pero kita naman eh.

267
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:03,233
Gusto mo rin si Joey.

268
00:13:03,367 --> 00:13:05,300
'Wag ako, Jin Ho.
Alam ko na 'yan.

269
00:13:07,467 --> 00:13:10,367
So do you think
I have a better chance?

270
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,700
Yes.

271
00:13:13,267 --> 00:13:14,667
But that's just what I think,
okay?

272
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:17,233
Why? Are you planning
to make a move on Joey?

273
00:13:17,367 --> 00:13:18,300
Just say it!

274
00:13:18,433 --> 00:13:19,667
No.

275
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:23,100
But still, you have to do
something about it.

276
00:13:24,233 --> 00:13:25,933
About it?

277
00:13:26,067 --> 00:13:27,467
What do you mean?

278
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:30,600
If your mindset is
how you present yourself,

279
00:13:30,733 --> 00:13:32,200
it won't happen.

280
00:13:32,333 --> 00:13:35,333
If you think I have a better
chance with Joey,

281
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,333
why don't you try
to be more like me?

282
00:13:39,567 --> 00:13:41,233
What do you mean?

283
00:13:47,567 --> 00:13:49,467
Mom, she's really not there.

284
00:13:50,033 --> 00:13:51,967
They told me she was
in the other room,

285
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:53,700
but she wasn't!

286
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:56,033
And Chief even drove me away.

287
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:57,333
I'm sure they're hiding
something,

288
00:13:57,467 --> 00:13:58,800
and Dad is alive.

289
00:13:58,933 --> 00:14:01,933
Child, why would Chief
lie to us?

290
00:14:02,067 --> 00:14:04,267
That's exactly what I want to
find out.

291
00:14:09,933 --> 00:14:11,367
Joey, my child...

292
00:14:14,967 --> 00:14:17,233
I know you're struggling,

293
00:14:17,367 --> 00:14:20,933
but you have to accept
that your father is gone.

294
00:14:23,433 --> 00:14:25,167
You see, Joey,

295
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:29,400
if what you're saying is true,
that he's alive...

296
00:14:29,567 --> 00:14:33,167
then he should already
be here with us.

297
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:36,233
He wouldn't be able to bear
seeing us in pain.

298
00:14:47,467 --> 00:14:48,467
I don't believe it, Mom.

299
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:50,300
I don't want to believe it.

300
00:14:51,833 --> 00:14:54,300
I think Dad is still alive.

301
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:58,533
Dad is still alive...

302
00:14:59,833 --> 00:15:01,467
Joey...

303
00:15:02,867 --> 00:15:04,633
My child, you'll only get hurt
even more

304
00:15:04,767 --> 00:15:07,100
if you don't accept it.

305
00:15:09,733 --> 00:15:11,867
It will hurt even more if you
don't accept

306
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,333
that your father is gone.

307
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:22,633
I don't want to, Mom...

308
00:15:58,533 --> 00:16:00,400
<i>- That's cute, isn't it?
- Yes.</i>

309
00:16:00,533 --> 00:16:01,900
<i>Keep this with you always, okay?</i>

310
00:16:02,033 --> 00:16:03,267
<i> Hang it on your bag</i>

311
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:06,867
<i>so even if I'm not by your side,
as long as you have this,</i>

312
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,133
<i>it'll feel like we're still
together.</i>

313
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:10,867
<i> Yes, that's true.</i>

314
00:16:11,267 --> 00:16:12,567
<i> Give me a smile.</i>

315
00:16:17,667 --> 00:16:19,700
<i> I know you're struggling,</i>

316
00:16:19,833 --> 00:16:23,600
<i>but you need to accept
that your father is gone.</i>

317
00:16:25,533 --> 00:16:28,267
Do I really have
to move on now, Dad?

318
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:32,700
Are you really gone?

319
00:16:34,033 --> 00:16:37,100
I thought we said never say die.

320
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:42,967
Dad, if you're still there,

321
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:45,667
give me a sign please.

322
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:52,900
Please, any kind of sign.

323
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:59,333
Just so I know if I should still
keep looking for you.

324
00:17:15,967 --> 00:17:18,967
Joey is still in denial
about her father's death.

325
00:17:21,667 --> 00:17:24,300
Just try to understand her.

326
00:17:24,433 --> 00:17:26,667
She's been through a lot.

327
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:28,467
I know that.

328
00:17:29,567 --> 00:17:33,233
But her plan to go up North,

329
00:17:33,367 --> 00:17:35,567
thinking she'll still find
her father...

330
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:39,567
I can't let her do that alone.

331
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:41,567
So what? You're going with her?

332
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:44,400
I know Joey.

333
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:47,267
She won't let herself
be stopped.

334
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:49,400
So...

335
00:17:49,567 --> 00:17:52,033
since when did Joey become
your responsibility?

336
00:17:52,167 --> 00:17:55,967
Major Delgado entrusted her
to me.

337
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:07,067
Our informant confirmed

338
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:09,433
that Delgado's body
was autopsied.

339
00:18:10,167 --> 00:18:12,100
I can't even call it
a cold corpse

340
00:18:12,233 --> 00:18:14,133
he was completely burned.

341
00:18:14,633 --> 00:18:18,367
At last, the thorn
in our side is gone.

342
00:18:18,867 --> 00:18:21,133
I put up with him
for a long time.

343
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:24,700
You can now focus on running
the warehouse.

344
00:18:25,267 --> 00:18:28,967
We need a lot of product
for our new stronghold.

345
00:18:30,533 --> 00:18:32,800
So things are really settled
between you and Delilah?

346
00:18:33,967 --> 00:18:36,400
She still wants to see me
in person.

347
00:18:36,967 --> 00:18:39,767
But once we meet,
the deal is sealed.

348
00:18:40,733 --> 00:18:44,867
Little by little, we'll crawl
our way into all the key cities

349
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:48,267
until we take the entire
Philippines.

350
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:54,133
Cheers.

351
00:19:01,433 --> 00:19:02,733
Sir.

352
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:07,600
Any news on Major Delgado's
DNA or autopsy?

353
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:09,800
Not yet.

354
00:19:09,933 --> 00:19:11,567
Just wait for the official
bulletin.

355
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:13,100
That's what everyone else
is doing anyway.

356
00:19:13,233 --> 00:19:16,100
Sir, I'm not doing this
for my report.

357
00:19:17,067 --> 00:19:20,300
I'm doing this for Joey
and Ms. Clarissa.

358
00:19:20,767 --> 00:19:23,633
You've seen how they're
grieving, right?

359
00:19:23,767 --> 00:19:26,200
Mr. Dizon,
you know the protocol.

360
00:19:26,333 --> 00:19:28,433
We can't just release
the results like that.

361
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:31,267
Sir, I'm not asking
for the full report.

362
00:19:32,467 --> 00:19:34,100
Wait, aren't you...

363
00:19:34,233 --> 00:19:36,000
you're close
to Major Delgado, right?

364
00:19:36,867 --> 00:19:39,067
Don't you care about his family?

365
00:19:41,567 --> 00:19:43,233
Sir, please.

366
00:19:43,367 --> 00:19:44,833
For Joey.

367
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:48,133
She's on the verge
of doing something reckless.

368
00:19:48,667 --> 00:19:51,433
She doesn't believe
her father is dead.

369
00:19:52,467 --> 00:19:54,700
She just needs to hear
something.

370
00:19:54,833 --> 00:19:56,767
She just need a confirmation.

371
00:19:57,800 --> 00:19:59,667
All right, all right, Sir.
I'll check.

372
00:19:59,800 --> 00:20:01,500
I'll call the Chief.

373
00:20:31,467 --> 00:20:33,000
Please, answer.

374
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:41,200
Hello?

375
00:20:41,333 --> 00:20:42,767
Why are you calling?

376
00:20:43,967 --> 00:20:45,600
<i>Don't worry,
I'm not leaving</i>

377
00:20:45,733 --> 00:20:47,933
because I can't
leave mom either.

378
00:20:48,067 --> 00:20:50,433
Joey, Joey, please, please
listen to me.

379
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,233
<i> Okay?</i>

380
00:20:52,967 --> 00:20:54,833
I'm starting to believe

381
00:20:54,967 --> 00:20:56,733
your father might still be
alive.

382
00:20:56,867 --> 00:20:57,967
What did you say?

383
00:20:58,100 --> 00:21:01,767
Okay, I overheard Cruz
and Lansang talking earlier.

384
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:04,700
<i> Sir, Andrew Dizon spoke to me.</i>

385
00:21:04,833 --> 00:21:07,467
<i>He's pressing
for the DNA confirmation.</i>

386
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:10,767
<i> You know what to say, right?</i>

387
00:21:11,700 --> 00:21:13,433
<i>He said he feels sorry for Joey.</i>

388
00:21:13,567 --> 00:21:15,533
<i> Actually, Sir, so do I.</i>

389
00:21:16,167 --> 00:21:19,600
<i>Sir, how long are we going
to hide this?</i>

390
00:21:20,433 --> 00:21:22,233
They're hiding something, Joey.

391
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:24,400
It's not clear to me yet
what it is,

392
00:21:24,533 --> 00:21:26,200
but they're not telling you
everything.

393
00:21:26,333 --> 00:21:27,767
<i> That's right, Andrew.</i>

394
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:29,167
That's why we keep asking
questions

395
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:31,667
because they're hiding
so many things...

396
00:21:32,233 --> 00:21:33,467
because Dad is still alive.

397
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:36,533
<i>Thank God, this is the sign
I've been waiting for.</i>

398
00:21:37,933 --> 00:21:39,400
I'm going to find Dad
no matter what.

399
00:21:39,533 --> 00:21:40,733
<i> Joey...</i>

400
00:21:40,867 --> 00:21:42,200
we.

401
00:21:42,367 --> 00:21:45,600
<i>We'll find your father together.</i>

402
00:22:05,267 --> 00:22:06,400
Just follow my advice.

403
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:08,633
Joey will stop noticing Andrew

404
00:22:08,767 --> 00:22:10,567
and start noticing you.

405
00:22:10,700 --> 00:22:11,967
What did you tell Ms. Clarissa?

406
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:13,800
I told her I just had something
to do at school.

407
00:22:13,933 --> 00:22:15,000
So now I'm thinking

408
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:18,400
maybe if I come home with Dad,
she'll understand me.

409
00:22:18,533 --> 00:22:20,533
Dad? Dad, wait! Dad!

410
00:22:20,667 --> 00:22:21,733
Why are you shouting
like that, huh?

411
00:22:21,867 --> 00:22:22,867
I'm just looking for someone.

412
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:23,700
Do you want us to help you?

413
00:22:23,833 --> 00:22:24,800
Let go of me!

414
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:27,500
Looks like your luck
just ran out, huh.

415
00:22:28,300 --> 00:22:29,600
I don't even know where to start

416
00:22:29,733 --> 00:22:31,267
once we get to Valmora.

417
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:33,033
I've got it covered,
I know someone in Valmora.

418
00:22:33,167 --> 00:22:33,833
Who?

419
00:22:33,967 --> 00:22:35,733
- Zoey.
- Andrew.
